meta {
  name: POST partner — watch the three console.logs
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/odata/v4/orders/BusinessPartners
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "acme corp",
    "country": "us",
    "industry": "Tech"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:4004
}

docs {
  ## Slide 4 — req.data — read, validate, mutate (Step 1: Read)

  Handler at this point (bare — just reading):

  ```js
  this.before('CREATE', 'BusinessPartners', req => {
    console.log(req.data.name)     // 'acme corp'
    console.log(req.data.country)  // 'us'
    console.log(req.data.region)   // undefined (not sent)
  })
  ```

  No validation, no mutation yet — this only reads. Watch the terminal:
  - `req.data.name` logs `'acme corp'`
  - `req.data.country` logs `'us'`
  - `req.data.region` logs `undefined` — it was never sent, and `region` isn't
    even a column on this entity; the point is just that an absent field reads
    as `undefined`, not `null` or an empty string.

  Expected: 201 Created. Nothing is rejected or transformed yet — that's next.
}
